---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { FOUNDER_COUNT, THRESHOLDS } from "../founding";

const next =
  THRESHOLDS.find((t) => FOUNDER_COUNT < t.count) ??
  THRESHOLDS[THRESHOLDS.length - 1];
---

<Base>
  <h1>The Santa Monica Athenaeum</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">
    A membership library for mathematics and philosophy in Santa Monica,
    California.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Why</h2>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        When evening has come, I return to my house and go into my
        study. At the door I take off my clothes of the day, covered
        with mud and mire, and I put on my regal and courtly garments;
        and decently reclothed, I enter the ancient courts of ancient
        men, where, received by them lovingly, I feed on the food that
        alone is mine and that I was born for. There I am not ashamed to
        speak with them and to ask them the reason for their actions;
        and they in their humanity reply to me. And for the space of
        four hours I feel no boredom, I forget every pain, I do not fear
        poverty, death does not frighten me. I deliver myself entirely
        to them.
      </p>
      <footer>
        — Niccolò Machiavelli, letter to Francesco Vettori, 10 December
        1513, in <em>The Prince</em>, trans. Mansfield (Chicago)
      </footer>
    </blockquote>
    <!--
      TODO: founder's letter goes here. Outline:
        1. The problem with LA's libraries — what the public system does
           well, and the kind of room it no longer provides.
        2. What this room is for — sustained reading, open shelves,
           conversation among members.
        3. Why now.
      Replace this comment and the paragraph below with the letter.
    -->
    <p><em>[Founder's letter — to be written.]</em></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The collection</h2>
    <p>
      Mathematics and philosophy, with an emphasis on primary texts: the
      works themselves, in good editions, rather than commentary alone.
      The shelves are open — members browse freely — and the collection
      lends. Nothing is behind glass.
    </p>
    <p>
      <!-- TODO: replace with the TinyCat catalog link or embed once live. -->
      The catalog will be browsable online at <a href="/collection/"
        >/collection</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Membership</h2>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Member</dt>
        <dd>$300 per year. Borrowing privileges and use of the reading room.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Founder</dt>
        <dd>
          $500 per year. Everything above, and your name on the founding
          plate.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Life</dt>
        <dd>$5,000, once. A member for good.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      Until our 501(c)(3) status is granted we are collecting
      <em>pledges</em>, not payments. No money changes hands until the
      Athenaeum can receive it properly.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/join/">Pledge a membership →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions</h2>

    <h3>What am I committing to when I pledge?</h3>
    <p>
      Your word, not your money. A pledge is a statement of intent — no
      card, no invoice, nothing binding. When the Athenaeum can properly
      receive funds, we will write and ask you to make it good, and you
      may decline then with no hard feelings.
    </p>

    <h3>When would I actually pay?</h3>
    <p>
      After the IRS grants our 501(c)(3) determination. We will write to
      every pledger with instructions at that point, and not before.
    </p>

    <h3>Where does the 501(c)(3) stand?</h3>
    <!-- TODO: keep this answer current as filings progress
         (incorporated → EIN → Form 1023 filed → determination). -->
    <p>
      We are forming a California nonprofit public benefit corporation
      and preparing the federal exemption application (Form 1023). This
      page will say so plainly at each step: incorporated, filed,
      granted.
    </p>

    <h3>Will my membership be tax-deductible?</h3>
    <p>
      Partially, in the usual way: the deductible portion of a
      membership is what you pay beyond the fair value of what you
      receive. Once our status is granted we will state the deductible
      amount for each tier in your written acknowledgment, per IRS
      rules.
    </p>

    <h3>What if the Athenaeum never reaches 25 founders?</h3>
    <p>
      Then no one pays anything. Pledges are only called in when the
      reading room can actually open. If we conclude it will not happen,
      we will write to say so and release every pledge.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I just send money now?</h3>
    <p>
      Not yet — we are not set up to receive charitable funds, and we
      would rather do this properly than quickly. Pledge, and we will
      call on you the moment we lawfully can.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Founding</h2>
    <p class="counter">
      {FOUNDER_COUNT} of {next.count} founders
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        THRESHOLDS.map((t) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{t.count} founders</strong> {t.unlocks}.
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .subtitle {
    text-align: center;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  dl div {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .counter {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
</style>
